ADDITIONAL NOTICE — READ BEFORE USING

This software routes traffic through a VPN you supply. It is offered with NO
WARRANTY THAT IT WILL KEEP YOU ANONYMOUS. Software fails, VPN providers log,
subscriptions lapse, kernels change, and misconfiguration is easy. Verify your
own installation with ./verify-anonymity.sh, and do not rely on this tool where
exposure would cause you real harm.

You alone are responsible for what you search for, download, and store. Hiding
traffic from an ISP does not make unlawful activity lawful. Copyright, computer
misuse, and privacy laws differ by country — know the rules where you live.

Never share your VPN configuration file. It contains a private key that is your
identity to the VPN provider, and traffic authenticated with it is attributable
to you.
